  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "Pippa made 1 litre of a drink containing apple juice and water mixed in a ratio of $3:2$. She found this too sweet so she made one litre of a drink mixed in a ratio of $1:2$. She found this to be too weak. What is the ratio of apple juice to water after she combines these two drinks?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p16-q23-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "7:8",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q23-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the apple juice volumes and the water volumes separately, then simplify their ratio.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "First drink:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Apple juice volume}&=\\frac{3}{5}\\times1=\\frac{3}{5}\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Water volume}&=\\frac{2}{5}\\times1=\\frac{2}{5}\\text{ L}\\end{align*}$$\nSecond drink:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Apple juice volume}&=\\frac{1}{3}\\times1=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Water volume}&=\\frac{2}{3}\\times1=\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ L}\\end{align*}$$\nCombined drink:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Apple juice volume}&=\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{14}{15}\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Water volume}&=\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{16}{15}\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Apple juice}:\\text{water}&=\\frac{14}{15}:\\frac{16}{15}\\\\\\text{Apple juice}:\\text{water}&=14:16\\\\\\text{Apple juice}:\\text{water}&=7:8\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
